      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to convert the base 5 numbers to base 10 and then sum them up to get the total dollar amount.\n\n1. **Convert \\( 3124_5 \\) to base 10:**\n   The number \\( 3124_5 \\) can be expanded as follows:\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot 5^3 + 1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 4 \\cdot 5^0\n   \\]\n   Calculating each term:\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot 5^3 = 3 \\cdot 125 = 375\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4 \\cdot 5^0 = 4 \\cdot 1 = 4\n   \\]\n   Adding these values together:\n   \\[\n   375 + 25 + 10 + 4 = 414\n   \\]\n   So, \\( 3124_5 \\) in base 10 is \\( 414_{10} \\).\n\n2. **Convert \\( 3122_5 \\) to base 10:**\n   Similarly, the number \\( 3122_5 \\) can be expanded as follows:\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot 5^3 + 1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 2 \\cdot 5^0\n   \\]\n   Calculating each term:\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot 5^3 = 3 \\cdot 125 = 375\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 5^0 = 2 \\cdot 1 = 2\n   \\]\n   Adding these values together:\n   \\[\n   375 + 25 + 10 + 2 = 412\n   \\]\n   So, \\( 3122_5 \\) in base 10 is \\( 412_{10} \\).\n\n3. **Convert \\( 124_5 \\) to base 10:**\n   The number \\( 124_5 \\) can be expanded as follows:\n   \\[\n   1 \\cdot 5^2 + 2 \\cdot 5^1 + 4 \\cdot 5^0\n   \\]\n   Calculating each term:\n   \\[\n   1 \\cdot 5^2 = 1 \\cdot 25 = 25\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot 5^1 = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4 \\cdot 5^0 = 4 \\cdot 1 = 4\n   \\]\n   Adding these values together:\n   \\[\n   25 + 10 + 4 = 39\n   \\]\n   So, \\( 124_5 \\) in base 10 is \\( 39_{10} \\).\n\n4. **Sum the base 10 equivalents:**\n   Now, we add the base 10 equivalents of the three numbers:\n   \\[\n   414 + 412 + 39 = 865\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total dollar amount that the pirate has accumulated is \\(\\boxed{865}\\).",
